 {:id :own-instance-sig-callstack
  :title "the own libraries' instance signatures push no call-stack frame"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "DsDoExprFailMsg and DsMonadCompFailMsg (compiled by the front end since HF10-P54; on the pack before) fail with GHC's message but their HasCallStack backtrace lacks the frame \"a type signature in an instance, called at .../Control/Monad/Fail.hs:65:13\": GHC checks `instance MonadFail IO`'s method against its instance signature `fail :: HasCallStack => String -> IO a` and pushes that origin onto the stack (tcMethodBody's InstanceSigOrigin), the elaborator ignores instance signatures (arbace.repr.haskell.typecheck's check-method takes the class's method type). Arbace's own ghc-internal's STG, not the programs'"
  :decided "gate B1 (2026-11-16, taken overnight): classed by what fails; instance signatures in the elaborator are the libraries' next gap"
  :outcome ":result :fail :status 1 :differs [:stderr]"
